  "summary_en": "Jordan's national AI policy issued by the Ministry of Digital Economy and Entrepreneurship. It sets five pillars (governance, legislation and regulation, digital infrastructure, business and investment, capacity building), creating a National Ministerial Committee, a National AI Ethics Charter, a regulatory sandbox, and incentives. It has no robotics-specific provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Creates a National Ministerial Committee for AI headed by the Minister of Digital Economy",
   "Requires a National Charter on AI Ethics covering accountability, transparency, impartiality and privacy",
   "Mandates a regulatory sandbox for AI applications in the public sector",
   "Classifies AI entities and offers tax and investment incentives",
   "Requires curriculum reform and workforce AI skills programmes"
  ],
